                <pb facs="0559" n="1213" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1213"/>

                <head>No. 557.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Young to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santiago
                                de Cuba</hi></placeName>. <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-12-18"><hi rendition="#italic">Dec</hi>. 18, 1873</date>.
                        (Received December 30.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 109 <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >bis.</hi>]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    complete list of the persons taken from on board the United States
                    merchant-steamer Virginius. I was present on board of the United States steamer
                    Juniata, at the solicitation of Commander D. S. Braine, when the remaining
                    prisoners were delivered on board this morning. Those checked are the persons
                    delivered, and those not checked are the names of those shot. I improve this
                    opportunity to send this direct, as the Juniata leaves for New York at 5 p.m.
                    to-day.</p>
                <closer><signed>A. N. YOUNG.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d258-a1.xml" xpointer="d258-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
